.FIRE WEATHER...
Issued at 429 AM PDT Fri Sep 11 2026

A new weather pattern will influence conditions over the Timber
and Plaskett Fires in Monterey County. The marine layer has
returned and is 1,600 feet deep as measured by the 12Z balloon.
This height should be fairly consistent through the day before
some expansion this weekend as the trough moves through. While the
marine layer brings much cooler and more humid conditions to the
coast, areas above the marine layer often experience nocturnal
drying as the dry air above the clouds rolls in simultaneously
with the low clouds. In the late morning the clouds will mix out
as the layers become less stratified, often increasing dew point
during the warmest part of the day.

